@AR 45. "Clothed with a talaris" (Revelation 1:13) = the proceeding Divine, which is the Divine truth. The reason "a talaris" (has this signification) is that "vestments," in the Word, = truths; hence "a talaris," which is a general vestment, when predicated of the Lord, = the proceeding Divine truth. @AC 6432[2]. @AE 64.

