@884. "God shall wipe away every tear from their eyes" (Revelation 21:4) = that the Lord will take away from them all grief of mind; for the shedding of tears is from grief of mind -animi-.

@CL 379[end]. The jealousy of a wife... is like grief weeping...

@SE 970[end]. (These) easily shed tears.

@4099. Inmost mercy is attended with tears.

@4976. Exhibiting the shedding of tears...

@5890. A Spirit who inflowed into the eyelashes of the left eye, which seemed as it were to emit tear drops... he was in external mercy...

@DMin 4782. (These infernals) tried to inspire... the shedding of tears...

@AE 484[2]. That "a tear from the eyes" = grief of mind on account of falsities, and from falsities, is because by "the eye" is signified the understanding of truth; and hence "a tear" = grief because there is no understanding of truth, consequently, because of falsities. Illustrated.

@--[3]. "The shedding of tears," and "weeping aloud -fletus-" both = grief on account of falsities and from falsities; but "the shedding of tears," grief of the mind -mentis-; and "weeping," grief of the heart. Explained, Illustrated. @695[16].

