Tent.; Tentorium.
Tent, To.; Tentoriare.
See <Tabernacle>, and <Temple>.

@AC 414. To "dwell in a tent" (Genesis 4:20) = the Holy of love. Illustrated.

@--. "Tent" = what is celestial. @--[2].

@471[end]. This is to "dwell in tents."

@1063. "The tents of Ham" (Psalms 78:51) = the worship therefrom. @3325[13].

@1074. "The midst of a tent" (Genesis 9:21) = the principal of faith; for "tent" = charity, or worship from charity. Charity is the inmost thing of faith and worship; and this is "the midst of the tent." That "tent" = the Holy of love, or charity. References.

@1102. "He shall dwell in the tents of Shem" (verse 27) = that the internals of worship may be in the externals.

@--. "Tents" = the Holy of love, and worship thence. To "sojourn and dwell in tents" was a wonted formula among the Ancients, by which was signified holy worship; for the reason that the Most Ancients not only sojourned with tents, but also dwelt in tents, and performed holy worship therein. @1293. @3312.

@--[2]. That "tents" = holy worship. Illustrated.

@1452. "He stretched his tent" (Genesis 12:8) = the holy things of faith; for "a tent" = the Holy of love, consequently the Holy of faith from love. His stretching his tent there = that this was now beginning.

@1556. "Even to the place where his tent was before" (Genesis 13:3) = to the holy things which there were before... "A tent" = the holy things of faith... thus the celestial things which the Lord had...

@1564. "(Lot) had flock, and herd, and tents" (verse 5) = the things with which the external man abounds.

@1566. "The tents" = the worship of that (external man) which was separating itself from the internal.

@--. "Tents," in the opposite, = worship not holy. Illustrated.

@1598. "He tented as far as Sodom" (verse 12) = extension to cupidities.

@1616. "Abraham tented..." (verse 18)... To "tent," that is, to move and fix a tent, = to be conjoined; for "a tent" = the Holy of worship, by which the external man is conjoined with the internal.

@2145. "He was sitting at the door of the tent" (Genesis 18:1) = the holy state of love in which He then was. @5152.

@2174. "A tent" = the Lord as to the Holy of love.

@2190. "Behold in the tent" (verse 9) = in what was holy, (Explained.)

@2195. "Sarah heard at the door of the tent" (verse 10) = that rational truth was near what was holy.

@2576[2]. "The tent," which was outside the ark, = the Lord's Kingdom.

@3210. "The tent of Sarah his mother" (Genesis 24:67) = the sanctuary of truth in the Divine Human. "A tent" = what is holy, thus a sanctuary.

@3268[5]. "Tents and flocks" = goods of the Spiritual Church.

@3312. "Dwelling in tents" (Genesis 25:27) = worship therefrom.

@--[2]. Hence it was commanded that they should make a tent...

@3322[4]. "The tent of David" (Amos 9:11) = the Church and worship of the Lord. ( = the good of love and of charity from the Lord. @4926[3].) @9163[end].

@3439[end]. Hence it was culled "the tent of meeting."

@3444. "Isaac stretched his tent there" (Genesis 26:25) = what was holy there.

@3540[3]. The tent was a representative of the three Heavens, thus of the celestial and spiritual things of the Lord's Kingdom.

@3762[4]. "Tents" = holy things of good.

@4128. "Jacob fixed his tent in the mount" (Genesis 31:25) = the state of that love.

@4153. "Laban came into the tent of Jacob, and into the tent of Leah, and into the tent of both the handmaids" (verse 33) = that in their holy things there were not such truths.

@4288[3]. In the representative Church they had tents or tabernacles, and Divine worship in them... because tents or tabernacles = the Holy of love and of worship.

@--[4]. They were therefore restricted... to a tent in common, which was called the tent of meeting.

@4391. Under <Hut>, see this reference.

@4398. "Where he had stretched his tent" = what was holy.

@4599. To "stretch the tent" = the progression of what is holy, here, towards interior things.

@4922[5]. As the tent of meeting with the ark represented Heaven...

@5135[6]. "Tent" = what is holy.

@8379. They have tents also in Jupiter. Described.

@--. They take their meals in their tents.

@8470. "Tent," here (Exodus 16:16) = a society as to good; for a tent here has the like signification to a house; for when they were sojourning they were in tents.

@8666. "They came into the tent" (Exodus 18:7) = the Holy of union... because love is union. Hence to "come into the tent" = to be united from holy love.

@9592. The Second Heaven is here represented by the habitation and the tent.

@9595. The curtains from the goats for the tent which was round about. @9615.

@--[2]. "Enlarge the place of thy tent" (Isaiah 54:2) = the Holy of worship from the good of love.

@--[3]. "My tents are laid waste" (Jeremiah 4:20) = holy worship from the good of love. ( = the Church. @9854[3].) @AE 724[16].

@9615. "The tent over the habitation" = the external of Heaven; for "the habitation" = Heaven; and the tent which covered it above = its external.

@9686. The Heaven which is represented by the tent of meeting...

@9784. "In the tent of meeting" (Exodus 27:21) = the Lord's presence; for the tent was made that the Lord might meet Moses and Aaron there, and also the sons of Israel; and on this account the Holy of worship was instituted there. Illustrated.

@9784[end]. For the tent represented Heaven; and Heaven is Heaven from the Lord's presence there.

@9854[2]. For the habitation, and the tent = Heaven.

@9963. "When they go into the tent of meeting" (Exodus 28:43) = in worship representative of all things of Heaven and the Church... For "the tent" represented Heaven where the Lord is... Moreover all the worship at that time took place in the tent...

@10001. "The tent of meeting" = Heaven.

@--[2]. "The altar" which was placed at the door of the tent, represented the Lord as to Divine good; and the tent of meeting represented the Lord as to Divine truth.

@10005[3]. As to the tent of meeting, by which is represented Heaven in which is the Lord... its inmost, where was the ark, represented the Third Heaven; the habitation, which was outside the veil, represented the Second Heaven; and the court, the First Heaven. @10268[2]. @10338. @AE 630[4]. @700.

@10022. "Before the tent of meeting" (Exodus 29:10) = for purification, the reception of truth from Heaven, and its conjunction with good; for "the tent of meeting" = Heaven where the Lord is.

@--. The place "before the tent," which is called its "door," = the conjunction of truth and good...

@10129[2]. The tent of meeting outside the veil represented the Spiritual Kingdom, or, what is the same, the Lord where He is present in the good of charity...

@10150. "I will sanctify the tent of meeting" (verse 44) = what is receptive of the Lord in the Lower Heavens. The reason "the tent of meeting" = the lower Heavens, is that "the altar" = the higher ones. Explained.

@10160[end]. Because the habitations of the Most Ancients were tents, a tent was constructed in memory of it which was used as a house of God, and the feast of tents was afterwards instituted in which they rejoiced from the heart.

@10206[end]. Next, the tent itself is described, by which is signified Heaven and the Church which is from the foregoing things.

@10230. "Thou shalt give it for the work of the tent of meeting" (Exodus 30:16) = conjunction with Heaven through the acknowledgement that all truths and goods are from the Lord... "The tent of meeting" = Heaven where the Lord is, thus also that which conjoins man with Heaven...

@10242. "In their entering into the tent of meeting" (verse 20) = worship from the good of faith. Explained.

@--[end]. For that tent (where Aaron and his sons made the daily ministration) represented the Heaven where spiritual good reigns.

@10268. "Thou shalt anoint with it the tent of meeting" (verse 26) = in order to represent the Divine of the Lord in the Heavens... "The tent of meeting" = Heaven in the whole complex. Explained.

@10304. "Thou shalt put of it before the testimony in the tent of meeting" (Exodus 30:36) = the worship of the Lord in Heaven and the Church... "The tent of meeting" Heaven; and (therefore) the Church also; for the Church is Heaven on earth.

@10338. "The tent of meeting and the ark for the testimony" (Exodus 31:7) = a representative of Heaven in general, where the Lord is. Explained.

@10545. "Moses took the tent" (Exodus 33:7) = the Holy of worship, of the Church, and of the Word; for "the tent," in the supreme sense, = the Lord, and also Heaven and the Church; and, in the relative sense, all the Holy of Heaven and the Church, and hence also the Holy of worship and the Holy of the Word... The reason "a tent" = these things, is that the Most Ancients dwelt in tents, and also held in them their holy worship...

@--[3]. That by "a tent" are signified these holy things;, and, in special, the Holy of worship. Illustrated.

@--[4]. "Tents" (Jeremiah 4:20) = the goods of the Church, "curtains," its truths.

@--[5]. As "tents" = the goods of the Church and of worship, therefore, in the opposite sense, "tents" = the evils of worship and of the Church. Illustrated.

@10546. To "stretch the tent" (Exodus 33:7) = to provide, dispose, and ordinate the things which are of the Church and of worship.

@10547. "Recalled it the tent of meeting" (Exodus 33:7) = the external of worship, of the Church, and of the Word, in which are internal things... "Meeting," in the sense of the letter, means the meeting (or assembly) of the sons of Israel; but in the internal sense is signified the assembly of the truths and goods of the church... @10548.

@10557. "The tent" = the Holy of the Word, of the Church, and of worship.

@10769. Their dwellings (in the Fifth Earth) were low houses in the form of tents, such as the ancients had. Described.

@CL 75[5]. A union like that of the two tents in the breast, which are called the heart and lungs.

@TCR 110. Two tents were seen, one directly above the place (where the meteor fell); and the other at the side, towards the south... A Spirit fell from Heaven and was cast into the (first) tent; and I was in the other... In the door of this I stood, and saw the Spirit in the other also standing in the door of his tent; and I asked him why he fell...

@AE 205[3]. The "tents of Judah" (Zechariah 12:7) = the Celestial Kingdom.

@223[16]. To "enlarge the place of the tent" = that they have worship from good. @600[12].

@324[3]. "The tent" = the Lord's Spiritual Kingdom; and that part of the tent which was within the veil = the Lord's Celestial Kingdom. Explained.

@365[40]. "Tents of securities" (Isaiah 32:18) = the derivative goods of love and of worship without infestation by evils and falsities.

@392[7]. "The tent of meeting" represented Heaven. @727[11]. @1042[5].

@412[8]. To "hide in Thy tent" (Psalms 31:20) = in the Divine truth.

@555[7]. "Ohola and Oholibah," that is, "the tent, or habitation of God;" for this = Heaven where are the Divine truth and the Divine good, and thence also the Church. @576[6].

@586[3]. The sacrifices at the door of the tent represented the worship of the Lord, because the altar, and also the tabernacle, represented Heaven where the Lord is present...

@630[4]. This was the court of the tent of meeting, (which last) represented Heaven.

@--. The three Heavens were represented by the tent. References. @700. @--[4], Explained. @--[33], Explained.

@654[56]. "Thorns shall be in their tents" (Hosea 9:6) = the falsity of evil in the worship.

@684[26]. "Surely I will not enter within the tent of my house" (Psalms 132:3) = that he will not enter into and know the holy things of the Church.

@700[33]. The primary representatives of the Lord, and thence of Heaven and the Church, were the tent of meeting... the altar... and afterwards the temple... with the difference that the tent of meeting was a more holy representative...

@724[17]. "The tents of Jacob" (Jeremiah 30:18) = all things of the Church... "tents" = its goods; "habitations," its truths.

@799[3]. "Tabernacle" = the Church from those in the good of love to the Lord; "tent" = the Church from those in truths from this good... Therefore "tabernacle" = the doctrine of the good of love; and "tent," the doctrine of truth from this good; thus "tabernacles," in the plural, = the goods of the Church and of doctrine; and "tents," the truths of the Church and of doctrine. Illustrated. @--[20].

@811[5]. "A tent" (Psalms 78:60) = the Church which is in the truths of doctrine.

Tent-companionship.; Contubernium.

@CL 290[end]. @297. @DWis 3. 4. (contubernales). @DWis 6. 7. (contubernium).

Terah.; Therach.

@AC 1353. "Terah" was a nation named from Terah as its father, by which nation is signified idolatrous worship. @1355. @1356, Explained. @1359.

@1356. Here it is very plain that Terah, Abram, and Nahor were idolaters.

@1357[end]. These three kinds of idolatry were signified by the three sons of Terah.

@1359. Terah was a son of Nahor, and also a nation named from him... @1362.

@1360. "These are the nativities of Terah" (Genesis 11:27) = the origins and derivations of the idolatry from which came the representative Church... Here a third Church after the Flood is treated of, which followed when the second became idolatrous in Terah. Terah, Abram, Nahor, and Haran were idolaters; and also the nations from them...

@1362. Terah was a nation from this: that the nations springing from his sons acknowledged him as their father. Explained.

@1363. Idolatry is signified by "Terah"...

@1366. Under <Haran (the man)>, see this reference.

@--. Terah and Abram worshipped other gods, and had no knowledge of Jehovah, nor therefore of what the good and truth of faith are. They had thus become better fitted to receive the seed of Truth than others in Syria. @1992[2].

@1367. Idolatrous worship in general is signified by "Terah."

@1373. "Terah took Abram his son; and Lot the son of Aaron... and Sarai... and they went forth with them from Ur of the Chaldees, to go into the land of Canaan" (verse 31) = that they who were in idolatrous worship were instructed in the celestial and spiritual things of faith, in order that a representative Church might thence come forth.

@1375. "And the days of Terah were 205 years; and Terah died in Haran" (verse 32) = the duration and state of that idolatrous worship; the end of that idolatry; and the beginning of a representative Church through Abram.

@3778. Terah, who was the father of three sons: Abram, Nahor, and Haran, represents the common stock from which the Churches were. Terah himself was indeed an idolater; but representatives do not regard the person... And, as the representative Jewish Church commenced in Abraham... therefore Terah and his three sons took on the representation of Churches... @4207.

@5628[2]. The family of Terah... acknowledged Shaddai as their god.

Teraphim.; Theraphim.

@AC 1356[2]. Laban worshipped images, or teraphim, which Rachel took away (Genesis 24:10; 31:19-34).

@4111. "Rachel stole the teraphim" = to take away the truths. @4149. @4151. @4153.

@--[4]. For "the teraphim" mean his gods. Illustrated.

@--[5]. The teraphim were idols which they employed when they consulted or interrogated God; and, as the answers they received were to them Divine truths, therefore truths are signified by those teraphim.

@--. "Ephod and teraphim" (Hosea 3:4) = the Divine truths which they received by the answers.

@--. "The teraphim" (Zechariah 10:2) = the answers, but in this state wrong ones.

@--[6]. As such things were signified by "teraphim," they were found with some, although prohibited. Illustrated.

@4155. "Rachel took the teraphim" (Genesis 31:34) = interior natural truths which are from the Divine... "Teraphim" = truths which are from the Divine.

@4162. "He searched, and found not the teraphim" (verse 35) = that those truths were not his. Explained.

@--[2]. That "the teraphim" = truths from the Divine, is because those who were of the Ancient Church distinguished the Divine... by various names... and the truths Divine which they received by answers they called teraphim... They who were wise among them understood by all these names the one only Lord; but the simple made for themselves so many representative images of that Divine... Hence came idolatry... But, as in ancient times Divine things had been understood by these names, some of them were retained, as teraphim, etc. By "teraphim" are signified truths Divine which came from answers, as is evident in Hosea 3:4.

@9824[end]. "Teraphim" = Divine answers. Illustrated.

Terebinth. See <Turpentine>.

Tergiversation.; Tergiversatio.
Refuse.; Tergiversari.

@AR 461. Faith alone induces evasion, etc., so that they do not think at all about the commandments.

@710. They evade reflecting upon (their) evils.

@SE 6106[2]. They want the wife to refuse. @6110[4].

Term. See <Boundary>.

Terminate. See <Boundary>.

Terraqueous.; Terraqueus.

@DLW 106. Our terraqueous globe.

@165. The terraqueous globe... is a kind of base and support; for it is the ultimate work...

@TCR 31. Of the terraqueous globe, regarded in itself, are predicated the things of space; and of its rotation and progression, are predicated those of time.

@33. Things at rest, of which the terraqueous globe consists.

@76[3]. At last... the terraqueous globe... was formed of earths... @78[4].

@769. When the universal firmament together with the terraqueous globe is expected to perish.

Terrestrial. See <Earthly>.

Terrible.; Terribilis.

@AC 3719. "How terrible is this place" (Genesis 28:17) = holiness of state... For the word "terrible," in the Original, is derived from the same word as "fear" (which) = what is holy.

@7573. But in Hell (truth Divine) is terrible.

@DLord 5. "The terrible" day = the advent of the Lord to Judgment.

@AE 556[5]. Because this state is profane and powerful, it is called "terrible," etc. (Daniel 7:7). @650[68].

@783[3]. Hence those in falsities are called "terrible," etc.

Territory.; Territorium. @SE 5759. b.

Terror.; Terror.
Terrify, To.; Terrere.
See <Dread>, and <Fear>.

@AC 390. They who are in falsity and evil are in continual terror lest they be killed. Illustrated.

@950[end]. A mere hiss would drive them into terror... They thought in their terror that all Hell was rising...

@955. From (these penalties) they contract terrors and horrors for such things.

@963[end]. Under the veil they feel such anxiety and terror...

@986. "The fear of you, and the terror of you" (Genesis 9:2) = the dominion of the internal man; "fear" regards evils; and "terror," falsities... For, when the internal man dominates, the man is in fear on account of evils, and in terror on account of falsities... But it is (only) the external man that is terrified... (Continued. See <Fear>.)

@1740[end]. (Evil Spirits) are sometimes seized with terror on their first approach (to such a man).

@1839. "A terror of great darkness" (Genesis 15:12) = that the darkness was terrible... ( = that He shuddered at so great a vastation. @--[3].)

@1951[end]. When Spirits merely think of such truth (without good), there arises something of terror. Explained.

@4555. "A terror of God was upon the cities..." (Genesis 35:5) = that falsities and evils could not come near; for "a terror of God" = protection. @--[2], Explained.

@--[end]. Not that the Lord terrifies them...

@4935. This naked arm... according to its position excites terror; in this position, incredible terror... Even those who have not been timorous... are thrown into extreme terror by it.

@5313[6]. "The lightnings," etc. = the terrors caused by the Divine truth with those who are not in good.

@5378[2]. They enlarged themselves, and thus terrified (those other Spirits).

@--[2]. For it is allowed the Spirits (of the peritoneum), when infested by others... to strike them with terror @SE 991.

@5502. Under <Tremble>, see this reference. @8312.

@7280[2]. From terror of the penalties.

@8316. "Terror took hold of them" (Exodus 15:15) = that they dared not attempt anything... For with those who are in terror, the blood grows cold, and rushes into the veins, and the circulation ceases; hence the nerves become flaccid, and the forces full, so that they dare not do anything.

@8816[end]. They who are in evil are in terror at the presence of the Divine...

@9327. "I will send My terror before thee" (Exodus 23:27) = the terror of those who are in evils of falsity on account of truths of good. Explained.

@9330[2]. When they are in Hell, they are in terror and consternation on account of the truths from good in which the Angels are...

@9331. Terror is predicated of those in evils; "dread -formido-" of those in falsities.

@AR 331. "A great earthquake" = ... terror, Explained.

@342[3]. They saw nothing but terrors before their eyes.

@517. "The rest became terrified" (Revelation 11:13) = from fear when they saw the destruction of others. ( = they were disturbed in mind and turned away. @AE 677.)

@936[end]. The leaves of these trees strike terror (there) when they are shaken by a strong wind; but not the leaves of the others.

@CL 263[2]. On seeing (that devil) I was terrified.

@SE 149. On the terror of those who have led a perverted life.

@996. That the Truth terrifies.

@--. In the other life, people can be struck with so much terror that they as it were melt away... even those who had lived almost devoid of terror. This terror comes forth from that Truth in which there is not goodness, or mercy; then such a terror penetrates the marrows, and as it were breaks the bones; for Truth condemns to the lowest Hell...

@1754. That there are those who strike terrors. - There are Spirits who trust in their own forces, who are sometimes permitted to induce terrors, incredible ones. They are permitted to represent a naked arm. (Explained.)

@1783. These were such as had formerly slain whole armies... for they rushed into the chambers of the brain, and injected such terror that one slew another... At this day however [they can do this] only a little (in certain cases of suicide). Explained.

@4756. How certain evil ones are reduced into terror, on account of evils they had perpetrated (here).

@DMin 4705. The crowd was dispersed, and so the terror (caused by those who correspond to cats) ceased.

@4780. The terror caused by those who are called the ast wind. Described.

@AE 395[9]. The consequent damnation is signified by "they shall be clothed with terrors..." (Ezekiel 26:16).

@453[11]. "Thine heart shall meditate terror..." (Isaiah 33:18) = remembrance of the state of the Church...

@677[4]. "Terror," and "consternation," in the Word, = a state of the lower mind disturbed and changed by an imminent or visible danger to the life; but this is one thing with the good, and another with the evil. Explained, Illustrated.

@--[8]. These passages (show) that "terror," and "dread," in the Word, mean various disturbances of the lower mind from such things as cause amazement, and which are conjoined also with joy.

@--[9]. Again, "terror" = terror on account of evils and falsities from Hell; for these terrify the spiritual man, because they are the opposites of goods and truths, which the spiritual man love, and the loss of which he fears. Illustrated.

@721[20]. "Terror on every side" (Jeremiah 4:25) = spiritual death.

@911[12]. "Terror" (Isaiah 17:14) = destruction.

Testament.; Testamentum.
See <New Testament>, and <Old Testament>.

@AC 9548[3]. "The two witnesses" = the Word of both Testaments, in so far as each testifies of the Lord.

@TCR 409. This makes a difference between the Old Testament, or Covenant, and the New.

@706[2]. The Word is called "a Covenant," and "a Testament," "Old," and "New;" thus the Divine truth there.

@AE 392[8]. See <Testimony>.

@936. "Moses and the Lamb" = the Word of the Old and New Testament. Explained.

Testicle.; Testis. Testiculus.
See <Spermatic>.

@AC 2468[15]. "Those who are wounded in a testicle" (Deuteronomy 23:1) = those who reject whatever is of love and charity.

@5060. Who correspond to the testicles was evident to me from those who are in contraries to conjugial love, and cause pain in the testicles. (These Spirits described.)

@TCR 584. See <Seed>.

@SE 3152. Those who love infants most tenderly... constitute a province in the quarter of the testicles and the dependent organs... @DeConj 100.

@5216. The inmost evil ones of the Babylonish religion inflowed into the testicles, and inflicted some pain on the interiors of them; a sign that they are utterly contrary to the interiors of Heaven.

@DMin 4582. Those who are more envious operate into the scrotum, and also into the ligaments towards the testicles.

Testify.; Testificare.
Testification.; Testificatio.

@AC 5028. Testification. Signified, Explained. @5654. @5919. @5920[end], Explained.

@7876. That this is a testification of the will of good. Signified, Explained.

@9293. For deeds are testifications of such things as as are of the will.

@DP 212[end]. Ocular testification.

@AR 960. The Lord... testifying this Gospel... Signified.

@CL 300[2]. These pledges are testifications. Explained.

@AE 706. A Divine testification concerning the future Church, and concerning the reception of its doctrine. Signified, Explained.

@--[4]. "Signs" = testifications which indicate and persuade... Illustrated.

@--[9]. Therefore a manifest testification was not given them from Heaven. Illustrated.

@--[12]. A testification that they might believe. Signified.

@824. Testifications and persuasions. Signified, Explained.

@826. To persuade... by testifications from the Word... Signified, Explained.

@838. A testification of acknowledgement that they are of the Church. Signified, Explained.

@CanonsNC 45. Trinity. 8. 4. A plurality of Gods may be confirmed by... "there are three that bear witness in Heaven..."

Testimony.; Testimonium.
Bear Witness.; Testari.

@AC 1038[5]. A covenant... was (therefore) established by the laws of society given from the Lord in the Jewish Church, called testimonies...

@2720[7]. "That it may be a witness unto me" (Genesis 21:30) = certainty.

@3478. The Lord Himself was represented by the testimony in the ark.

@3488[8]. "For a testimony" (Matthew 24:14) = that they may know, and not make it a pretext that they have been ignorant.

@4195. "_Jegar-sahadutha_" means "the heap of witness," in the idiom of Syria. Explained.

@4197[3]. "A witness -testis-" = confirmation of good through truth, and of truth by good; and hence "a testimony" = the good from which is truth, and the truth which is from good. Illustrated. @--[8], Illustrated. @--[9], Explained.

@8535. "Aaron laid it up before the testimony" (Exodus 16:34) = that it was in the Divine presence... "The testimony" = the Divine... because, in the universal sense, "the testimony" means the Word; and the Word is truth Divine, thus the Lord.

@--[2]. That "the testimony" = the Lord as to Divine truth, is evident from the ark in which was the Law... which is called "the testimony." That the tabernacle derived all its sanctity from it; and that the testimony was the Holy Divine itself, is evident from...

@9410[5]. "The word of their testimony" (Revelation 12:11) = truth Divine received by man. @9503[2].

@9455. The testimony, or Law, in the ark, represented the Lord. @9482.

@9485. The reason the testimony, or Law, in the ark = the Lord, is that "the testimony" = Divine truth, (which) is the Lord in Heaven.

@9503. "Thou shalt put the testimony to the ark" (Exodus 25:16) = the Divine truth, which is the Lord in Heaven. "The ark" = Heaven; and "the testimony," the Divine truth, thus the Lord in Heaven. @9519. @9524.

@--[2]. A distinction is made in the Word between "laws," "statutes," "judgments," "precepts," "testimonies," etc... as in "the testimony of Jehovah is firm, making wise the simple"... From these things it may be evident that "testimony" = the Divine truth, which bears witness concerning the Lord; thus the Word; for this, in the supreme sense, treats of the Lord alone, and then, in the internal sense, bears witness concerning Him, that is, teaches Him, and the truths of faith and goods of love which are from Him. Illustrated.

@--[3]. That the Divine truth which proceeds from the Lord is called "the testimony" from the fact that it testifies concerning the Lord. Illustrated... To "this end came I into the world, that I may bear testimony to the Truth."

@9680[2]. "The testimony" = the Lord as to Divine truth. @9785. @10304. @10375. @10451.

@9682. "The testimony" = the Lord. @AE 283[14]. @727[11].

@9818[22]. "The testimony of Jesus" (Revelation 19:10) = the Divine truth which is from Him and about Him.

@10196. "The testimony" = the Lord as to the Word.

@10206[2]. "The testimony" is described first, by which is meant the Lord.

@DLife 57. This Law is called "a covenant" because it conjoins; and "a testimony" because it bears witness...

@62. "False testimonies," etc. with the concupiscences to them, are the sins which are to be shunned. Explained.

@87. In proportion as anyone shuns false testimonies of every kind as sins, he loves the Truth. General article. @AE 949[3].

@--. To "bear witness falsely." Defined.

@AR 6. "Who bore witness to the Word of God, and to the testimony of Jesus Christ" (Revelation 1:2) = who from the heart, and thus in light, receive Divine truth from the Word, and acknowledge the Human of the Lord to be Divine... The Angels bear witness, that is, see, acknowledge, and receive from the heart in light, and confess, the truths of the Word; especially this truth: that the Human of the Lord is Divine. @35. @AE 10, Explained. @52.

@--[2]. As to the spiritual signification of "bearing witness," it is predicated of the Truth, for the reason that in the world the Truth is to be borne witness to; and, when it has been borne witness to, it is acknowledged. But in Heaven the Truth itself bears witness concerning itself, because it is the very light of Heaven... And, as the Lord is the Truth itself... He is, in Heaven, the testimony of Himself. Hence it is evident what is meant by "the testimony of Jesus Christ." Illustrated.

@325. "The souls of them that were slain... for the testimony which they held" (Revelation 6:9) = those hated and rejected by the evil on account of... their acknowledgement of the Lord's Divine Human. @AE 392.

@--. In Heaven, testimony is given solely to those who acknowledge the Lord's Divine Human; for the Lord is He who bears witness, and He gives to the Angels to bear witness.

@490. That the Lord is the God of Heaven and earth, and that His Human is Divine, is "the testimony." Illustrated.

@--[2]. And that the second essential of the New Church, which is conjunction with the Lord by a life according to the commandments, is also "the testimony." Illustrated.

@499. "When they shall have finished their testimony" (Revelation 11:7) = after the Lord has taught that He is the God of Heaven and earth, and that there is conjunction with Him by a life according to the commandments. ( = at the end of the Church, when the Divine of the Lord is no longer acknowledged, and hence there is no longer good of love and truth of doctrine. @AE 649.)

@555. "They overcame him... by the word of their testimony" (Revelation 12:11) = victory... through the acknowledgement that the Lord is the God of Heaven and earth, and that the precepts of the decalogue are precepts of life according to which men must live. ( = through the confession and acknowledgement of the Divine in His Human. @AE 749). @AE 329[20].

@--. "Testimony" = the Divine Truth; in especial, these two things.

@565. "The remnant of her seed, who keep the commandments of God, and have the testimony of Jesus Christ" (verse 17) = novitiates, who receive the doctrine concerning the Lord, and concerning the decalogue. ( = who acknowledge the Divine in the Lord's Human. @AE 770.)

@669. "The temple of the tabernacle of the testimony" (Revelation 15:5) = the inmost of Heaven, where is the Lord in His Holiness in the Word, and in the law which is the decalogue. ( = interior Divine truth in the Word revealed by the Lord. @AE 948).

@--[2]. That the law which is the decalogue was called "the testimony." Illustrated. @AE 392[6].

@818. "I am of thy brethren who have the testimony of Jesus" (Revelation 19:10) = ... that he is in conjunction with the Lord, through the acknowledgement of the Divine in His Human, and a life according to His commandments. @AE 1230.

@819. "For the testimony of Jesus is the spirit of prophecy" (Revelation 19:10) = that the acknowledgement that the Lord is the God of Heaven and earth, together with a life according to His commandments, is, in the universal sense, the all of the Word and its derivative doctrine. Explained. @AE 1232.

@846. "The souls of them that were beheaded for the testimony of Jesus" (Revelation 20:4) = those rejected... because they had worshipped the Lord, and had lived according to the truths of His Word. Explained.

@TCR 149. "The testimony of Jesus" = confession from faith in Him.

@285. This Law is called... "the testimony," because it confirms the articles of the covenant; for... "testimony," in the Word, = the confirmation and witnessing of the articles of (conjunction).

@AE 10. For to "bear witness" = to acknowledge at heart.

@27[2]. To "bear witness." and "testimony." Illustrated.

@392[4]. That "testimony" = confession of the Lord; and the Lord Himself. Illustrated. @--[7].

@--[5]. That "testimony" = the Lord; and, with man, the confession of the Lord from the heart; and in in special, the acknowledgement of the Divine of the Lord in His Human. Illustrated. @--[9], Illustrated.

@--[8]. Hence the Word before the Lord's advent is called "the old Covenant;" and that after His advent, "the New Covenant;" it is also called "the Testament, Old and New;" but it should be called "the Testimony."

@--[11]. "Testimony" = that in the Word which teaches goods of life; "law," that which teaches truths of doctrine. Illustrated.

@803[2]. "False witness." Defined. (See @TCR 321.)

@1050. "The testimony of Jesus" = the acknowledgement of the Divine of the Lord in His Human; and that He alone is to be worshipped and adored.

Tetter.; Vitiligo.

@AE 962[10]. The Jewish nation was afflicted with such things (as tetter) on account of their profanations of the Word... @AC 7524[3].

Text.; Textus.

@AC 71. The things in the text of the Word.

@5578. In the Original... the text was continuous, in imitation of the heavenly speech.

@7933[end]. The internal text is so connected -continens- that not a syllable could be omitted...

@DLW 260. All the interior tissues would be scattered.

@SE 4671. When the Word is read by man in the Hebrew text. @DeVerbo 4.

@AE 1085[3]. For this reason there has been no mutilation... not even in a word or letter in the original text.

@DeVerbo 4[end]. All the letters in the Hebrew text were counted by the Masorites.

